ll-explanation"><p>Correct options:</p>

<p>Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) is a web service that provides=
 secure, resizable compute capacity in the cloud with support for per-secon=
d billing. It is the easiest way to provision servers on AWS Cloud and acce=
ss the underlying OS.</p>

<p>Amazon EC2 differs fundamentally with the traditional on-premises hostin=
g systems in the flexibility, control and significant cost savings it offer=
s developers, allowing them to treat Amazon EC2 instance as their own custo=
mized server backed by the robust infrastructure of AWS Cloud.</p>

<p><strong>Amazon EC2 can scale with changing computing requirements</stron=
g></p>

<p>When computing requirements unexpectedly change, Amazon EC2 can be scale=
